      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can argue that the increased compliance costs will strain the budget of mid-sized manufacturers, potentially leading to reduced competitiveness against larger, more established firms. Operationally, transitioning to new, greener technologies often requires significant capital investment and downtime, which directly impacts production schedules and output volume. Furthermore, overly stringent targets could unintentionally drive up operational expenses through the need to adopt specialized, potentially expensive emission control equipment. Finally, there is a risk that sudden, steep regulatory shifts may not align with realistic technological timelines for achieving compliance.",
